The Shrewd Dude schrieb:
> 
> Trivia #102
> 
> More Streaking
> -Three strikes, and you're out.

I didn't see you specify that rule before posting the previous run.

> 1. When a troll revives, can its gender change?

Mu. If a troll has gender, s/he isn't 'it' in the first place.

> 2. Eating a monkey may give what sort of resistance?

Eating a 'k' monster may give poison resistance. Eating any other 'm',
'o', 'n', 'k', 'e' or 'y' monster will not give anything labelled a
resistance.

> 3. This type of giant is considered the most dangerous.

By whom? 
Anyway, my vote goes to: giant mimic.

> 4. Polymorphing out of Xorn form may leave you in a what?

Quandary.

> 5. Complete this sentence: "Ask not what your magic can do..."

"... for you, ask what you can do for your magic!"

> 6. Who/what might say the following?
> 
> Yeah, you and me
> Are the best I can wish for
> To have with me in the dungeon.

A saddled succubus speaking to a bullwhip-wielding archeologist.

> 7. Dust clouds have what sort of detrimental effect?

They impede respiration.
Alas, they don't exist in Nethack.

> 8. What effect does a black light's attack have on another monster?

Makes anything white it's wearing glow like it's fluorescent.

> 9. Arch-liches have a base level of ____.

Same as chameleons ... five?

> 10. The Wizard of Yendor's maximum level is ____.

The plane of water.

> 11. Who/what might say the following?
> 
> All the girls find me attractive.
> I'm brawny and muscular.
> Maybe the radiation therapy did work?
> But when I stare deeply into their eyes...
> Never mind.

Arnold Schwarzenegger.

> 12. Complete this sentence: "Og friend. Og good dude..."

"... Og still owe me many-many-plus-one mammoth bones."

> 13. Complete this sentence: "There's a slip of paper inside. What a
> pity..."

"... it's an old Yendorian Lottery Ticket."

> 14. In the Rogue level, coins appear as what symbol?

The one that was formerly known as Prince.

> 15. True or false: Demonbane does double-damage against all "&".

Grayswandir's much better.

> 16. A beaked polearm is the description for what sort of item?

A weapon.

> 17. True or false: Eating a yeti always gives you cold resistance.

Eating a yeti always gets you a very pissed-off WWF.

> 18. An elven leather helm is described as a what?

"Elven leather helm". Ask any barbarian, knight, samurai, valkyrie or
elf.

> 19. True or false: Eating a former pet horse will have negative
> consequences.

For the horse, yes.

> 20. You feel entrapped! Besides a confused scroll of gold detection,
> applying what item might give you this message?

Nothing. The message is not given with an exclamation mark.

> 21. Polymorphing a % will always produce a %.

The number of items coming out of a large polypile is usually only a
%age of the input.

> 22. True or false: "You choke on the fortune cookie -more-"

"it reads: Eating too large a meal can be hazardous to your health."

> 23. True or false: "Never play leapfrog with a herd of unicorns!"

Alas, 'j'umping towards a unicorn only tells you you can't stamp on
it.

> 24. True or false: "They say that a nymph will be pleased if you call
> her by her real name."

Typical nymph names can be found in any source on greek mythology.

> 25. True or false: "They say that a minotaur will get lost outside of
> the mazes."

I'd better ask the local Arch-Lich what she thinks of that.

